  "response": "I’m using the repository’s `crimes-codebase-risk` workflow to ground the proposal in the exact repeated JSX and preserve the intended scan-driven refactor process.\n\nThe finding is `crime_00064`: it pinpoints the action footer—not the status controls—as the four-way duplicate. I’m checking the two dashboard example boundaries before choosing whether the component should be shared across both apps or duplicated once per independently runnable example.\n\nThe relevant result is `crime_00064`, `duplicate_component_shape`. It identifies the repeated footer `<div>` containing the Cancel link and submit button across all four invoice forms.\n\nProposed component: `InvoiceFormActions`\n\n```tsx\ntype InvoiceFormActionsProps = {\n  submitLabel: React.ReactNode;\n  cancelHref?: string;       // defaults to \"/dashboard/invoices\"\n  cancelLabel?: React.ReactNode; // defaults to \"Cancel\"\n\n  slots?: {\n    cancelAction?: React.ReactNode;\n    submitAction?: React.ReactNode;\n  };\n};\n```\n\nThe component owns the shared wrapper layout, Cancel link styling, and default `<Button type=\"submit\">`. The optional slots allow either action to be replaced without copying the enclosing subtree. It should not expose `className`; keeping the layout internal is what prevents drift.\n\nUsage:\n\n```tsx\n<InvoiceFormActions submitLabel=\"Create Invoice\" />\n<InvoiceFormActions submitLabel=\"Edit Invoice\" />\n```\n\nFiles that change:\n\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx`\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx`\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx` — new\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx` — new\n\nAlthough the scan groups all four occurrences, `final-example` and `starter-example` are independent Next.js applications. I would mirror the same component